[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Class 5 Single Segment High Risk Security Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @vcr_grammar

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document specifies cybersecurity requirements for Class 5 vehicle components: **Single Segment High Risk**.

Class 5 devices are truck modules connected to a single vehicle network segment found to have a high overall fleet risk based on system criticality and vehicle operational impact.

Examples include:
- Power TakeOff (Front or Secondary) (J1939 SA 07)
- Idle Control System (J1939 SA 68)
- Pneumatic System Controller (J1939 SA 48)
- Power TakeOff (PTO) Switches (J1939 SA 07)
- Engine Cylinder Pressure Monitoring System
- Aftertreatment #1 / #2 system gas intake (J1939 SA 81, 86)
- Diesel Particulate Filter Controller / Aftertreatment Control Module (ACM) (J1939 SA 211)
- Engine Exhaust Backpressure (J1939 SA 34)
- Retarder - Driveline / Exhaust / Engine (J1939 SA 16)
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Baseline Security Requirements Applicability

